  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Nitrobenzene part converts to aniline part using&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Sn</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>HCl</mi></math>. Aniline forms diazonium salt with nitrous acid and hydrogen chloride. Diazonium salt forms phenol with warm water.Phenol forms poly substituted bromo compound with bromine water.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0006_5a8a8c31fca4.png\" style=\"width: 750px; height: 266px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0006_885ab26fe907.png\" style=\"width: 600px; height: 317px;\" /></p><p>The compound P, on reaction with phenol gives coupling reaction and gives a coloured dye.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0005_3dacc0964ec0.png\" style=\"width: 494px; height: 416px;\" /></p><p>Total number of carbon atoms in S are 42 and hetero atoms are 9(Nitrogen and oxygen).</p></blockquote>"
